[38;2;124;124;124mAt degree $n$ (for $n \geq 3$), we need to find $p_{n-1}, q_{n-1}$ homogeneous [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mof degree $n-1$ such that:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$u \cdot q_{n-1} + v \cdot p_{n-1} = h_n$$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mwhere $h_n = \delta_n - \sum_{i+j=n, 2 \leq i,j \leq n-2} p_i q_j$ is a known [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mhomogeneous polynomial of degree $n$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe map $\psi: k[u,v]_{n-1} \times k[u,v]_{n-1} \to k[u,v]_n$ given by $(p, q) [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mapsto v \cdot p + u \cdot q$ is surjective for $n \geq 2$ (where $k[u,v]_m$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdenotes homogeneous polynomials of degree $m$).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mProof of surjectivity: $k[u,v]_n$ has basis $u^n, u^{n-1}v, \ldots, uv^{n-1}, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mv^n$. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $v \cdot k[u,v]_{n-1}$ is spanned by $vu^{n-1}, vu^{n-2}v, \ldots, vv^{n-1}$, [0m[38;2;124;124;124mi.e., $u^{n-1}v, u^{n-2}v^2, \ldots, v^n$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $u \cdot k[u,v]_{n-1}$ is spanned by $u \cdot u^{n-1}, u \cdot u^{n-2}v, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\ldots, u \cdot v^{n-1}$, i.e., $u^n, u^{n-1}v, \ldots, uv^{n-1}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTogether, these span $u^n, u^{n-1}v, \ldots, uv^{n-1}, v^n$, which is all of [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$k[u,v]_n$. So the map is surjective. ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, for $n = 3$: $h_3 = \delta_3$ (since there are no $p_i q_j$ terms with $i +[0m[38;2;124;124;124mj = 3$ and $i, j \geq 2$). We find $p_2, q_2$ with $v p_2 + u q_2 = \delta_3$. ✓[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mFor $n = 4$: $h_4 = \delta_4 - p_2 q_2$. We find $p_3, q_3$ with $v p_3 + u q_3 [0m[38;2;124;124;124m= h_4$. ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAnd so on. The induction proceeds.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, the formal power series $p = \sum_{n=2}^{\infty} p_n$ and $q = \sum_{n=2}[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m^{\infty} q_n$ are well-defined elements of $k[[u,v]]$ (each coefficient of $u^a[0m[38;2;124;124;124mv^b$ is determined by finitely many terms, specifically only $p_n$ with $n = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124ma+b$).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe have $X = u + p, Y = v + q$, and:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$XY = (u+p)(v+q) = uv + uq + vp + pq$$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe need to verify $uq + vp + pq = \delta$. By construction, the degree $n$ part [0m[38;2;124;124;124mof $uq + vp + pq$ equals $\delta_n$ for each $n \geq 3$, and is 0 for $n \leq 2$[0m[38;2;124;124;124m(since $p, q \in (u,v)^2$ means $uq, vp \in (u,v)^3$ and $pq \in (u,v)^4$). And [0m[38;2;124;124;124m$\delta \in (u,v)^3$ so $\delta_n = 0$ for $n \leq 2$. So $uq + vp + pq = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\delta$. ✓[0m

